      "lowerIsBetter": true,
      "verdict": {
        "winnerId": "electron",
        "headline": "Electron moved JSON across the boundary 1.81 times faster than Tauri over 1 KB, 64 KB, 1 MB and 16 MB (geometric mean of medians)",
        "summary": "Size by size, Tauri over Electron: 1 KB 5.9x slower, 64 KB 1.6x slower, 1 MB 1.2x slower, 16 MB 1.1x faster. The raw bytes path is the finding on this machine: WebView2 hands 16 MB back in 377 ms where Electron takes 65, about five times slower, and the Mac's WKWebView does the same job in 9. Same Rust host. I didn't chase why; that's a Tauri-on-Windows question, and it's the one to ask before you pick a shell for a data-heavy app. Push held its rate on both."
